From 326911734dadd7217466d941eae45c43d184d3c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:13:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] Bound every gateway request by one whole-operation
 deadline; make close terminal across gateway, roots and helper

Root's loopback repro (root-witness-deadline-review) on 7b4e8c68 (gateway sha256 e33d8a4b) used maxInFlight 1, a
150 ms deadline and 3 concurrent reads. The third read reached the upstream at 222 ms and still returned success at
324 ms. Causes:
- ask() computed the remaining time before waiting for the limiter;
- the limiter's wait was unbounded and could not be cancelled;
- nothing bounded cache, root or helper work by the request deadline.

* network/witness-gateway.mjs:
  - Each handle() runs under one operation context {signal, deadline}. The signal aborts at the deadline or on
    close(), and expiry is also judged by time. No success is returned after the deadline, and no upstream request is
    started after it, broadcasts included. A broadcast that reached k upstreams before the deadline reports that
    without returning a late result.
  - Limiter (FIFO, maxInFlight, maxQueued):
    - a waiter whose signal aborts is removed at once, and never reaches an upstream;
    - the try budget is computed when the slot is GRANTED, and no try starts with less than minTryMs (25 ms) left;
    - a slot is released only when the underlying work settles, so a source that ignores abort still counts against
      maxInFlight, and its late answer is discarded.
  - fetch gets AbortSignal.any([request, per-try timeout]); aborting also cancels the body read.
  - Helper checks, root lookups and ancestry walks get the request signal.
  - Cache:
    - reads have their own budget (cacheTimeoutMs), so a slow cache is skipped, not waited out;
    - verified writes run in the background, capped by maxCacheOps, and settled() awaits them. A hanging cache never
      stalls or fails a verified read.
  - close() is TERMINAL: queued and running requests end at once, new requests are refused, and background writes get
    at most 1 s.
  - The P2P comment is corrected to the evidenced bound: pinned/current Base defaults disable state serving with no
    flag; no enabled supported path was observed; custom peers were not ruled out.
* network/witness-verify.mjs:
  - abortable() helper.
  - checker.check(request, {signal}): an abort drops only that check, so a shared helper is never killed for one
    caller.
  - checker.close() is terminal: no restart, and the old child's output and exit are ignored. Crash/hang restarts
    are unchanged.
  - Root store:
    - rootFor(hash, {headers, deadline, signal}) awaits the shared poll abortably;
    - a shared ancestry walk is reference-counted and runs under its own controller and the latest caller deadline.
      It stops (no more header fetches or checks) when its last caller leaves, and is never joined after it was
      abandoned;
    - headers(hash, child, {signal, deadline});
    - offer(commitment, {signal});
    - close() is terminal: it aborts the poll and walks, discards a late answer, and stops polling.
    - Bindings already made stay: they are immutable history, not freshness.
* test/witness-deadline.test.mjs (11 tests over loopback HTTP; real helper and real recorded witnesses; labelled
  SEAMs only to force hangs):
  - root's repro on the new code, plus the NEGATIVE CONTROL on the exact 7b4e8c68 source (sha checked);
  - a request expiring in the queue, and no late success;
  - an abort-ignoring fetch;
  - no transaction sent after the deadline;
  - hanging cache read and write;
  - per-request abort on the real shared helper, and terminal checker close;
  - a hanging helper check isolated from a concurrent read;
  - gateway close while queued;
  - root store close with a late poll;
  - shared walk refcount and stop.
* Existing tests now await settled() before inspecting the cache. The hung-sources bound test expects a deadline
  refusal.
